Feature: Unity Catalog Schema Design for purgo_playground

  Background:
    Given the schema is named "purgo_playground"
    And the context is to store sales data from multiple regions

  Scenario: Create the schema with necessary tables
    Given the database system supports Unity Catalog
    When the schema "purgo_playground" is created
    Then a table named "sales_data" should exist
    And the table should have columns "country_cd", "product_id", "qty_sold", "sales_date"

  Scenario Outline: Validate data values and formats for sales_data table
    Given a new row is created in "sales_data" table
    When the following data is inserted
      | country_cd | product_id | qty_sold | sales_date |
      | <country_cd> | <product_id> | <qty_sold> | <sales_date> |
    Then the "country_cd" should be a valid ISO country code
    And the "product_id" should match the format "P####" where #### is a number
    And the "qty_sold" should be a positive integer
    And the "sales_date" should follow the format "YYYY-MM-DD"

    Examples:
      | country_cd | product_id | qty_sold | sales_date  |
      | US         | P1001      | 50       | 2024-01-15  |
      | CA         | P1003      | 25       | 2024-01-17  |
      | UK         | P1004      | 20       | 2024-01-19  |

  Scenario: Error when inserting invalid data in sales_data table
    Given the table "sales_data" exists
    When incorrect data with "country_cd" as "INVALID" is inserted
    Then an error message "Invalid country code" should be displayed

    When incorrect data with "product_id" as "1001" is inserted
    Then an error message "Invalid product_id format, should be P####" should be displayed

    When incorrect data with "qty_sold" as "-10" is inserted
    Then an error message "Quantity sold must be a positive integer" should be displayed

    When incorrect data with "sales_date" as "15-01-2024" is inserted
    Then an error message "Invalid date format, should be YYYY-MM-DD" should be displayed

  Scenario: Check user roles and access control
    Given user roles are defined
    When a user with role "analyst" accesses the schema
    Then the user should have read-only permissions on "sales_data" table

    When a user with role "admin" accesses the schema
    Then the user should have read-write permissions on "sales_data" table

  Scenario: Integration with existing systems
    Given a connection to the existing data warehouse
    When data is transferred to the "purgo_playground" schema
    Then the data should comply with the defined formats and rules

  Scenario Outline: Data update process and frequency
    Given the existing data is present in the "sales_data" table
    When new sales data is acquired
    And the data update occurs with frequency "<frequency>"
    Then the table should be updated accordingly

    Examples:
      | frequency |
      | daily     |
      | weekly    |

  Scenario: Generating reports from the schema
    Given the schema "purgo_playground" is populated with data
    When a report is generated on sales by country
    Then the report should display correct and formatted data

  Scenario: Project timeline and milestones
    Given the project has defined objectives
    When the project timeline is created
    Then it should include key milestones for schema creation, data integration, and report generation
